// Hand-written answers Lio gives to common questions (used by js/qa.js together with js/qa-seeds-more.js).
// Format, one object per answer:
//   id:   short unique name
//   q:    3-6 example phrasings of the question readers might type; a reader's question is matched
//         against the phrasings of every answer by word similarity (js/qa.js, seedFor), so write
//         them the way readers ask, casual and formal, short and long, and keep them distinct from
//         other answers' phrasings (`node tools/seed_check.js --collisions`)
//   a:    the answer HTML; src: where the facts come from
//   not:  optional words that must not appear in the question; notPhrase: phrases that must not
// Every fact must be checked against the paper (assets/paper.pdf); a fact not in the paper has no answer here.
// Parts starting with "Paper ·" carry section, table or figure numbers (they link into the paper).
// Check changes with `node tools/seed_check.js` (probes, --lint, --suggest, --precision, --collisions)
// and `node tools/qa_eval.js`.
